{"title":"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(uses_calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (uses calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3a_(Same_Solution_but_Explained_More)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3a (Same Solution but Explained More)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For any sequence of real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3ee662d1e7f2ede2bfb906763473851494e0240.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A=(a_1,a_2,a_3,\\ldots)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"147\" height=\"18\" />, define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/819a22695f39b0a9f752568347867b1d5d724ad0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta A^{}_{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"19\" /> to be the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/4/e24d8ad641a44e613fb0eefda8cf038dd6b0825e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_2-a_1,a_3-a_2,a_4-a_3,\\ldots)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"227\" height=\"18\" />, whose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a8aced58caf290c8d6f37e6aca43e0a13158dfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^{\\mbox{th}}_{}$\" width=\"26\" height=\"19\" /> term is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/a/7ea8434c71428a370c279c33fd445d39823d3b1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1}-a_n^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"75\" height=\"12\" />. Suppose that all of the terms of the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/9/3b9e249d12727e2ae58b3e1bef718ee2b7fc4912.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta(\\Delta A^{}_{})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"57\" height=\"18\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/c/6fcf4632fcaec896cdfbce2fc3a897e43e1f3ec4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^{}_{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"12\" />, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/3/9f30c2cdc96f22e6f8291bc8bed17eb63df6b3a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{19}=a_{92}^{}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"104\" height=\"17\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d94776d2f0b85bdf6d6eab811425151c1bd0fff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1^{}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"15\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28uses_calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(uses_calculus)\">Solution 1 (uses calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (uses calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a737670d481129e2ead6d7223437f3cf70ea53f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />s are reminiscent of differentiation; from the condition <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/6/346a1e1c17d3a923fb6dca132a200c68a2a6b0c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta(\\Delta{A}) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"18\" />, we are led to consider the differential equation\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/0/af013df2791580cc580e82a31f8161d69c45d4c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{d^2 A}{dn^2} = 1\\]\" width=\"65\" height=\"39\" />\nThis inspires us to guess a quadratic with leading coefficient 1/2 as the solution; \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed5b3cb947b54a5625700ea6654971d8d953025.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{n} = \\frac{1}{2}(n-19)(n-92)\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"37\" />\nas we must have roots at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aeed81ffe5071b2d5d291bca220b3480da708cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/d/42db13061b8fbe234757157c4c479d2f4b5f6fb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 92$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/9/c69f3320d5aa37f32a2b9fe394a3416b4c18f899.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=\\frac{1}{2}(1-19)(1-92)=\\boxed{819}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"245\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/1/7617f2e3239dfd874d2834442ff1d98a0d29c67f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta^1 A=\\Delta A$\" width=\"89\" height=\"15\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/c/f6c773537ecc15362e0402a2414c3245413434fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta^n A=\\Delta(\\Delta^{(n-1)}A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"155\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Note that in every sequence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/2/412787c048e28774dc63fc27db42dc52ca858de7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/8/338fb7983782e482693114d82ab49bf04f7581c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=\\binom{n-1}{1}\\Delta a_n + \\binom{n-1}{2}\\Delta^2 a_n +\\binom{n-1}{3}\\Delta^3 a_n + ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"450\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/0/5a04637775d7107f4f2f9fb9a36e372e69adc870.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=a_1 +\\binom{n-1}{1}\\Delta a_1 +\\binom{n-1}{2}\\Delta^2 a_1 +\\binom{n-1}{3}\\Delta^3 a_1 + ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"485\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/d/47d9a14c631f24f2ae681c7195c0943d8b6768c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta a_1 =a_2 -a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/6/50652a3727b0986065af760b4b68d96c6ff952de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n=a_1 +\\binom{n-1}{1}(a_2-a_1) +\\binom{n-1}{2}\\cdot 1=a_1 +n(a_2-a_1) +\\binom{n-1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"571\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5c318671c44014d314d9d243c3190d084ad0057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{19}=0=a_1+18(a_2-a_1)+\\binom{18}{2}=18a_2-17a_1+153$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"446\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/3/a2307be98e38e94e7519dd9ee221ac617e72712f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{92}=0=a_1+91(a_2-a_1)+\\binom{91}{2}=91a_2-90a_1+4095$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"455\" height=\"55\" />\n</p><p>Solving, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86a37b7418254c1bd292f81d01d65cec781f2c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=\\boxed{819}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b566e6ca3a04c18c2c6a67e158f66412c1c766e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta(\\Delta A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> is the second finite difference sequence, and the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> terms of this sequence can be computed in terms of the original sequence as shown below.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/e/12e2db67820b00754c97386ec204fb4eb1296c14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{array}{rcl} a_3+a_1-2a_2&amp;=&amp;1\\\\ a_4+a_2-2a_3&amp;=&amp;1\\\\ &amp;\\vdots\\\\ a_k + a_{k-2} - 2a_{k-1} &amp;= &amp;1\\\\ a_{k+1} + a_{k-1} - 2a_k &amp;=&amp; 1.\\\\ \\end{array}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -50px\" width=\"209\" height=\"109\" />\n</p><p>Adding the above <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dc6fab4c2fdb4e9046030fbfdcf6ea721b05602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> equations we find that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/5/7c5c7d639ddad5bd38d6e3525e58c99038cc404f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a_{k+1} - a_k) = k-1 + (a_2-a_1).\\tag{1}\\]\" width=\"363\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We can sum equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/7/5e7a1b6098a8c98b8e4adae526aeef4b91712620.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, finding\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/8/32826ecc2a25d0c2d49d33af6157f62e4a8029c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[18(a_1-a_2) - a_1 = 153.\\tag{2}\\]\" width=\"329\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>We can also sum equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd34ff50f8bba26a08bc96a69e921daa60f5f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, finding\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/a/83a3e395db14255a97fc5cc4f090e8d88eec4ced.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[91(a_1-a_2) - a_1 = 4095.\\tag{3}\\]\" width=\"335\" height=\"18\" />\nFinally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/3/ca379795bb61cd4feca43e839f9457bd35d0696b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18\\cdot (3) - 91\\cdot(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" /> gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86a37b7418254c1bd292f81d01d65cec781f2c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=\\boxed{819}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>Kris17\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3a_.28Same_Solution_but_Explained_More.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3a_(Same_Solution_but_Explained_More)\">Solution 3a (Same Solution but Explained More)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3a (Same Solution but Explained More)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Start with this (from Solution 3):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/3/24378bfacc83654539fbd07ae917209eec4a80e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{array}{rcl} a_3-2a_2+a_1&amp;=&amp;1\\\\ a_4-2a_3+a_2&amp;=&amp;1\\\\ a_5-2a_4+a_3&amp;=&amp;1\\\\ &amp;\\vdots\\\\ a_k-2a_{k-1}+a_{k-2} &amp;= &amp;1\\\\ \\end{array}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -53px\" width=\"216\" height=\"115\" />\n</p><p>When every equation is added up, most terms cancel to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/8/5b8098b0f1275c07c5549302658fa7cac308e5fe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k-a_{k-1}-a_2+a_1=k-2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"221\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Now add up this series of equations:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/5/cd5ae0deb979c7ed598a77a39222b8ebdf9955ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{array}{rcl} a_{92}-a_{91}-a_2+a_1&amp;=&amp;90\\\\ a_{91}-a_{90}-a_2+a_1&amp;=&amp;89\\\\ a_{90}-a_{89}-a_2+a_1&amp;=&amp;88\\\\ &amp;\\vdots\\\\ a_{20}-a_{19}-a_2+a_1&amp;=&amp;18\\\\ \\end{array}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -53px\" width=\"232\" height=\"115\" />\n</p><p>Again, most terms cancel or can be added up to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/c/70cf6f9de2b7f62500c13844e32a690002b76c47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{92}-a_{19}+73(-a_2+a_1)=\\frac{(90+18)(90-18+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"401\" height=\"40\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c5130f0ed99992574952ff05a31f3dad8e43c5af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\therefore -a_2+a_1 = 54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"132\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Using the original equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d208179b7d4fc364c0219580791a9c0fcaa43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k-a_{k-1}-a_{k-1}+a_{k-2}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"224\" height=\"18\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3359f43f0fd0ed3b672d389374aecd0360921a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> substitute to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f90c277a40a1efc7f17b2c336a0be5a083316c37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-a_3+a_2=53$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>Now substitute this equation for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/a/eeae143c5c9dbd376ffa1ffa8bdb93a58e8c9889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" /> and continue until <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8be368eeaa364432c1ebb74b8a18f7913a80b3f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/c/1bcea64b28de70cec86961378e046529ab757987.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{array}{rcl} -a_3+a_2&amp;=&amp;53\\\\ -a_4+a_3&amp;=&amp;52\\\\ -a_5+a_4&amp;=&amp;51\\\\ &amp;\\vdots\\\\ -a_{19}+a_{18}&amp;=&amp;37\\\\ \\end{array}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -53px\" width=\"168\" height=\"115\" />\n</p><p>Terms cancel until <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/4/ff412a909e65019f1a5f89d3b7c3bad514ad2cfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-a_{19}+a_1 = \\frac{(54+37)(54-37+1)}{2} = 819$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"335\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f931886d2bb143b586cd6a0cf52599e6d3430321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{19} = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"59\" height=\"17\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86a37b7418254c1bd292f81d01d65cec781f2c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=\\boxed{819}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n~unhappyfarmer\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since all terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/5/8b566e6ca3a04c18c2c6a67e158f66412c1c766e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta(\\Delta A)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"56\" height=\"18\" /> are 1, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a8053f0d9394bf8aadf203cf519ce5f2531ba270.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Delta A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> looks like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/4/9e4646eaaeb88c1668d132a1e8b0d7de8b8756b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(k,k+1,k+2,...)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"144\" height=\"18\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> looks like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f3c8bd7ca98d77ce2787386c9ad5e6dd7d9b61e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a_1,a_1+k,a_1+2k+1,a_1+3k+3,a_1+4k+6,...)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"403\" height=\"18\" />. More specifically, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/3/e833a2e4e6d95fe3383672850f99d4daa30342dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A_n=a_1+k(n-1)+\\frac{(n-1)(n-2)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"290\" height=\"38\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/5/af50cec3f1da65d1dff6c96839716d495853f1c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{19}=a_{92}=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"107\" height=\"17\" />, we have the following linear system: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b71b27bca9295942d1c4ecf2ccc0b6df441c59.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1+91k=-4095\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"15\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/a/4aa48dcc019073f914215f30a90ecd6c0c3591f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1+18k=-153\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"15\" /> From this, we can easily find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/2/002699c37d03e8e64613232c210a9faee76606eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=-54$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86a37b7418254c1bd292f81d01d65cec781f2c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=\\boxed{819}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"23\" />.\nSolution by Zeroman\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since the result of two finite differences of some sequence is a constant sequence, we know that sequence is a quadratic. Furthermore, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fad30f005ec63ad73fc3e3e10623add267c3c9d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(19) = f(92) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" /> so the quadratic is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/8/ca883e27cc97f32c99107eb0e3d7ee508d4c1dac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = a(x-19)(x-92)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"197\" height=\"18\" /> for some constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45ef9cdc7c7d46920eac603663914e0d9261a99b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> Now we use the conditions that the finite difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/e/45ef9cdc7c7d46920eac603663914e0d9261a99b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> We know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/4/6d400480febe140f48604df620d214ca0fb60743.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(19) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"76\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/a/f9ac850096cd32718dc58abda3bf9b839f188696.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(20) = -72a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/7/ab73a5c9c8caa2a36a9b4097e5eb47e32b88a4e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(18) = 74a.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"20\" /> Therefore applying finite differences once yields the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/1/38166b47e2b2888a16dd9b5d9c050bb79864caa6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-74a,-72a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"91\" height=\"15\" /> and then applying finite differences one more time yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6ea4756efa52a156029529aba37a305a5cb496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/0/8b08b708c54fe44a46aaf6668e7fcfe9619f620d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a =\\frac{1}{2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"50\" height=\"37\" /> Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/a/38ab1288b70252b6a45e1cc4d5badcc4946da47e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = 9 \\cdot 91 = \\boxed{819}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c47eead52a47b31decfb68f69c9e7b88b7219ca6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1=a,a_2=b.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> From the conditions, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2ad1f22692b4c8e2571649a4940ea4f97fc24b3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{n-1}+a_{n+1}=2a_n+1,\\]\" width=\"180\" height=\"16\" /> for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ea0b84f7cf916258a52e571a45582ab49c12f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" /> From this, we find that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/373c0f8d9cf0c0279b1292e84c79f8950af24ddd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} a_3&amp;=2b+1-a \\\\ a_4&amp;=3b+3-2a\\\\ a_5&amp;=4b+6-3a, \\end{align*}\" width=\"134\" height=\"66\" />\nor, in general, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cf1bf8468a86ac2cf8ee0b3362e64af8a44e3ce.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n=(n-1)b+\\frac{(n-2)(n-1)}{2}-(n-2)a.\\]\" width=\"336\" height=\"38\" /> Note: we can easily prove this by induction. Now, substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/d/dad1ecdfcc6bcbf0cf0c3795c125e1b81f854fdb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=19,92,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> we find that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bf532da132ec434ab0403207fae83ac77c3ff34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 0=&amp;18b+\\frac{17\\cdot18}{2}-17a\\\\ 0=&amp;91b+\\frac{90\\cdot91}{2}-90a\\\\ b=&amp;\\frac{17a-\\frac{17\\cdot18}{2}}{18}=\\frac{90a-\\frac{90\\cdot91}{2}}{91}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"232\" height=\"128\" />\nNow, cross multiplying, we find that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/7/8d77414ccf90c7f5e0623ff1272e65c31e1b535a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 91\\left(17a-\\frac{17\\cdot18}{2}\\right)&amp;=18\\left(90a-\\frac{90\\cdot91}{2}\\right)\\\\ 1547a-\\frac{(18\\cdot91)\\cdot17}{2}&amp;=1620-\\frac{(18\\cdot91)\\cdot90}{2}\\\\ 73a&amp;=\\frac{18\\cdot91}{2}\\cdot(90-17=73)\\\\ a=\\frac{18\\cdot91}{2}=9\\cdot91=\\boxed{819}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"423\" height=\"174\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME\" title=\"1992 AIME\">1992 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1992 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1992\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1992_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1992 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017180047\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.051 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.067 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 526/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 17260/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.145      1 -total\n 58.65%    7.709      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.51%    5.194      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2918:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017180047 and revision id 283127. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}